      {"kind": "text", "slot": "title", "rect": [120, 182, 1000, 150], "style": "Release Title", "sample": "Kestrel Bay Ferries launches the first fully electric crossing to Marrow Island"},
      {"kind": "text", "slot": "subtitle", "rect": [120, 340, 1000, 80], "style": "Deck", "sample": "The forty minute route will save around 4,000 tonnes of carbon a year and adds two daily sailings for island residents."},
      {"kind": "line", "from": [120, 448], "to": [1320, 448], "stroke": {"color": "tint", "weight": 1}},
      {"kind": "image", "slot": "hero", "rect": [120, 484, 760, 430]},
      {"kind": "text", "slot": "caption", "rect": [120, 926, 760, 40], "style": "Caption", "sample": "Tern, the first of two battery-electric vessels, on sea trials off Gull Point in August."},
      {"kind": "text", "flow": "body", "rect": [120, 980, 760, 290], "style": "Body", "sample": ["PORT ELLIS, 7 October 2026. Kestrel Bay Ferries today launched the first fully electric passenger and vehicle crossing between Port Ellis and Marrow Island, replacing two diesel vessels on the island's busiest route.", "The new vessel, Tern, carries 300 passengers and 60 cars and recharges in eleven minutes at each end of the crossing from shore batteries fed by the island wind farm. The route will run fourteen times a day, two more sailings than before, from 6:00 until 22:30.", "Island residents have been involved since the project began in 2023, helping to shape the timetable, step-free boarding and the new waiting rooms at both terminals."]},
      {"kind": "rect", "rect": [120, 1304, 4, 148], "fill": "accent"},
      {"kind": "text", "slot": "quote", "rect": [150, 1298, 730, 120], "style": "Release Quote", "sample": "Tern is quieter, cleaner and more reliable than anything we have sailed before. It is the biggest change to island life in a generation."},
      {"kind": "text", "slot": "quotecredit", "rect": [150, 1428, 730, 24], "style": "Quote Credit", "sample": "Rowan Achebe, Chief Executive, Kestrel Bay Ferries"},
      {"kind": "text", "flow": "body", "rect": [120, 1486, 760, 520], "style": "Body", "sample": ["The company expects the route to save around 4,000 tonnes of carbon each year, roughly the annual emissions of 900 homes. Noise in the harbour has also fallen sharply, which local wildlife groups hope will help the seal colony at Gull Point.", "A second electric vessel, Petrel, is under construction at the Ardmore yard and will join the fleet in the spring of 2027, when the overnight freight service will also switch to battery power.", "Fares are unchanged. Tickets can be booked online, through the app or at either terminal, and island residents continue to travel at the community rate.", "Ends", "Notes to editors", "Tern was designed by Halvorsen Marine and built at the Ardmore yard. She is 74 metres long, and her batteries hold enough charge for three crossings in a row.", "Photographs and a fact sheet are in the press kit. Interviews with the crew and the island community trust can be arranged through the media contact."]},
