      {"kind": "text", "rect": [960, 1318, 360, 20], "style": "Side Label", "text": "About the company"},
      {"kind": "line", "from": [960, 1348], "to": [1320, 1348], "stroke": {"color": "ink", "weight": 1}},
      {"kind": "text", "slot": "summary", "rect": [960, 1364, 360, 260], "style": "Boiler", "sample": "Kestrel Bay Ferries has connected Port Ellis with Marrow Island and the outer skerries since 1952. The company runs six vessels and carries 1.2 million passengers a year, and has committed to a zero-emission fleet by 2030. It is owned by the island community trust and employs 340 people on both sides of the water."},
